## Contract snapshot

The files under `platform/` are versioned, byte-identical snapshots of
golden-path `ai.platform/v1` schemas, copied when this project was
generated. The runtime validates `capability.yaml` against this local copy,
so it does not depend on the golden-path tooling.

A released `ai.platform/v1` schema is immutable. Your team *can* technically
edit this snapshot today, and nothing detects that yet. A later golden-path
verification step is intended to detect contract and provenance drift.

## Platform-managed fields

`api_version`, `kind` and `metadata.template_version` in `capability.yaml`,
and the files under `platform/`, are managed by the golden path. Do not
edit them by hand.

## Not generated by this template version

Template {{ template_version }} does not generate:
- a real provider adapter;
- a model-based judge, embeddings or similarity scoring;
- an OpenTelemetry SDK or exporter, a collector, or any network telemetry;
- a durable or tamper-proof audit log;
- latency timeouts;
- a tool runtime or policy hooks;
- CI.

Passing tests and a green eval gate mean the runtime enforced the boundaries
listed above, and the declared eval expectations held, with a deterministic
fake model. They do not show that any real model produces good
explanations, or that this capability is safe or production-ready.
